course: dictionary
lesson: 14367
title: Oppressed: treated unfairly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Oppressed» means treated in a cruel and unfair way by people who have power over you, and not given your freedom or rights. «The villagers were oppressed by a cruel ruler who took their food.» The clues are cruel, took and unfair, so oppressed must mean treated badly by someone in charge.
explain: The word can also describe a feeling. «The heat was so strong that Sam felt oppressed and could hardly move.» Nobody is being cruel to Sam here. The heat is weighing him down, so oppressed means weighed down by something, such as worry, sadness or heat.
explain: Use the swap check. In the heat sentence, "treated unfairly" does not fit, but "weighed down" does. In the ruler sentence, "weighed down" sounds wrong, but "treated unfairly" makes sense. Choosing the meaning that fits the clues is how you solve it.
fact: «Oppressed» means treated cruelly and unfairly by people with power.
fact: «Oppressed» can also mean weighed down by worry, sadness or heat.
fact: «The oppressed» means people who are treated unfairly by those in power.
fact: Enslaved people, people under dictators and groups denied rights have all been called oppressed, and people have fought against oppression to win freedom.
fact: In the Bible, the Israelites were oppressed in Egypt, and God led them out in the story of the Exodus.
exercise: «The villagers were oppressed by a cruel ruler who took their food.» What does oppressed mean here? | *Treated cruelly and unfairly by someone with power | Singing loudly at a festival | Very well fed and happy | Lost in a forest
exercise: «The heat was so strong that Sam felt oppressed.» What does oppressed mean here? | Cold and wet from the rain | *Weighed down, as if the heat was pressing on him | Happy and free to play
exercise: Which phrase means people who are treated unfairly by those in power? | *the oppressed | the powerful | the rulers | the free
test: «Many people in history were oppressed by dictators who denied them their rights.» What does oppressed mean? | *Treated unfairly and denied their rights | Given many gifts | Out of breath after running | Rich and famous
test: «The Israelites were oppressed in Egypt until God led them out.» What does oppressed mean? | Trained as soldiers | Happy in the sunshine | Asleep for many years | *Treated cruelly and unfairly, and not free
exam: Which sentence uses oppressed to mean weighed down by worry or heat? | The oppressed people marched to the capital city | The soldiers oppressed the villagers for many years | *Mia felt oppressed by the sticky heat all afternoon | Dad oppressed the bread dough until it rose
